Subject: [PATCH] Port LLVH support code to WASI

WASI libc has no process spawning, mapped memory, password database or
signals. Guard the LLVH code that needs them: mapped-memory and mapped-file
calls return an unsupported error, ~user expansion and the main executable
lookup do nothing, and Program.cpp, Signals.cpp and Watchdog.cpp include
WASI implementations (Signals.inc and Watchdog.inc come in the next patch).
Also add the <exception> and <type_traits> includes that the WASI libc++
headers do not pull in.

Upstream: not submitted. Needed only for a WASI target.
